Description: CVE-2026-54241 - Fix heap OOB read from int32 overflow in SAO buffer-size calc
 libde265's apply_sample_adaptive_offset_sequential() in libde265/sao.cc computed
 the SAO input buffer size as image_stride * height * bytes_per_pixel using signed
 32-bit int arithmetic. With sufficiently large HEVC frame dimensions that still
 pass SPS validation (e.g. pic_width=pic_height=46341 at 16-bit depth), the
 multiplication overflows INT32_MAX and wraps to a small positive value, producing
 an undersized heap allocation. The SAO filter subsequently reads past that buffer
 using the original (non-wrapped) stride, resulting in a heap out-of-bounds read
 (CWE-190 / CWE-122).
 .
 This backports only the CVE-2026-54241-specific portion of upstream commit
 bdca87569b9c63c2a7054d90ae4462dbb78d159a: the size computations for
 lumaImageSize/chromaImageSize are widened to size_t and the per-channel stride
 used in the memcpy is widened to ptrdiff_t / cast to size_t, so the buffer-size
 arithmetic is performed in a wide-enough type and no longer overflows. The
 unrelated pixel-accessor changes from that combined commit (which address the
 sibling CVE-2026-54240) are intentionally excluded.
Origin: upstream, commit:bdca87569b9c63c2a7054d90ae4462dbb78d159a
Author: Root.io Security Team <security@root.io>
Last-Update: 2026-07-18
---
--- a/libde265/sao.cc
+++ b/libde265/sao.cc
@@ -343,25 +343,25 @@ void apply_sample_adaptive_offset_sequential(de265_image* img)
     return;
   }
 
-  int lumaImageSize   = img->get_image_stride(0) * img->get_height(0) * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(0);
-  int chromaImageSize = img->get_image_stride(1) * img->get_height(1) * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(1);
+  size_t lumaImageSize   = static_cast<size_t>(img->get_image_stride(0)) * img->get_height(0) * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(0);
+  size_t chromaImageSize = static_cast<size_t>(img->get_image_stride(1)) * img->get_height(1) * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(1);
 
   uint8_t* inputCopy = new uint8_t[ libde265_max(lumaImageSize, chromaImageSize) ];
   if (inputCopy == NULL) {
     img->decctx->add_warning(DE265_WARNING_CANNOT_APPLY_SAO_OUT_OF_MEMORY,false);
     return;
   }
 
 
   int nChannels = 3;
   if (sps.ChromaArrayType == CHROMA_MONO) { nChannels=1; }
 
   for (int cIdx=0;cIdx<nChannels;cIdx++) {
 
-    int stride = img->get_image_stride(cIdx);
+    ptrdiff_t stride = img->get_image_stride(cIdx);
     int height = img->get_height(cIdx);
 
-    memcpy(inputCopy, img->get_image_plane(cIdx), stride * height * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(cIdx));
+    memcpy(inputCopy, img->get_image_plane(cIdx), static_cast<size_t>(stride) * height * img->get_bytes_per_pixel(cIdx));
 
     for (int yCtb=0; yCtb<sps.PicHeightInCtbsY; yCtb++)
       for (int xCtb=0; xCtb<sps.PicWidthInCtbsY; xCtb++)
Description: CVE-2024-38950 - Resize window if image resolution changes mid-stream
